# _shared/kern.fea
# Kerning feature (§10).
# Kern pairs are class-based and live in each master's kerning.plist, grouped by
# the public.kern1/public.kern2 groups in the same UFO. ufo2ft's kern feature
# writer turns those into GPOS at compile time.
#
# The "# Automatic Code" line below is that writer's insertion marker, and it is
# load-bearing: without it ufo2ft decides the feature is hand-maintained and
# *drops the UFO's kerning entirely* ("font has kerning, but also manually
# written kerning features without an insertion comment"). This file used to hold
# 27 hand-written pairs and no marker, so every pair in kerning.plist was being
# thrown away in favour of that shorter list. The pairs it had that the class
# table lacked — L before T/V/W/Y, and f before i — moved into KERN_PAIRS in
# tools/strike/build_t1_glyphs.py.
#
# Add manual exceptions below the marker, never above it, and never re-state a
# pair the class table already covers: both lookups would apply and the kern
# would be taken twice.

feature kern {
    # Automatic Code
} kern;
